00:04:14,285 --> 00:04:20,285
The battle for the lawn is on.

2
00:08:28,571 --> 00:08:34,571
The Ant Bully is a fantasy, adventure, animation film directed by John A. Davis.

3
00:12:42,857 --> 00:12:48,857
Fed up with being targeted by the neighborhood bully, 10-year-old Lucas Nickle
vents his frustrations on the anthill in his front yard ...

4
00:16:57,142 --> 00:17:03,142
until the insects shrink him to the size of a bug with a magic elixir.

5
00:21:11,428 --> 00:21:17,428
Convicted of "crimes against the colony," Lucas can only regain his
freedom by living with the ants and learning their ways.

6
00:25:25,714 --> 00:25:31,714
Lucas Nickle (voice), played by Zach Tyler Eisen.

7
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Hova (voice), played by Julia Roberts.

8
00:33:54,285 --> 00:34:00,285
Queen (voice), played by Meryl Streep.

9
00:38:08,571 --> 00:38:14,571
Zoc (voice), played by Nicolas Cage.

10
00:42:22,857 --> 00:42:28,857
Stan Beals (voice), played by Paul Giamatti.

11
00:46:37,142 --> 00:46:43,142
Fugax (voice), played by Bruce Campbell.

12
00:50:51,428 --> 00:50:57,428
The Ant Bully is a 2006 American animated fantasy comedy film
written, directed, and co-produced by John A.

13
00:55:05,714 --> 00:55:11,714
Loosely based on the 1999 children's book of the same name, it tells the story of Lucas Nickle, a young
boy who, after terrorizing a colony of ants, is shrunken and ordered to work amongst them.

14
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
The film was produced by Legendary Pictures, Playtone, and DNA Productions, and features the voice talents of Julia
Roberts, Nicolas Cage, Meryl Streep, Paul Giamatti, Regina King, Bruce Campbell, and Zach Tyler Eisen.

15
01:03:34,285 --> 01:03:40,285
Released on July 28, 2006, by Warner Bros.

16
01:07:48,571 --> 01:07:54,571
Pictures, The Ant Bully received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $55 million
against a $50 million budget, making it a box-office disappointment.

17
01:12:02,857 --> 01:12:08,857
This led to extensive layoffs at DNA Productions
and, ultimately, the studio's closure.

18
01:16:17,142 --> 01:16:23,142
The Ant Bully was Ricardo Montalbán's final film role before his death in 2009.

19
01:20:31,428 --> 01:20:37,428
The film explores themes of ant-hill, ant, child hero, shrinking, bully.

20
01:24:45,714 --> 01:24:51,714
The tone is lighthearted.
